viewpoints, but there are many reasonable restrictions that don't 
involve viewpoints.  Resource abuse, forgeries of posts and cancels,
forging moderator approval, etc.  In fact, I would be among the first
to step to the plate to criticize gmitchell's site should they yank his
account for his "eat a worm and die" post, despite the fact that there
are many who would interpret this as a death threat, and gleefully be
