net.  I don't do this kind of shit.  I even commented unfavorably on
his nomination to the Usenet Kook of the Month awards (nomination based
on his view that spamming should be considered protected free speech),
because I happen to think this is trivializing what is an important
question for Usenetters to examine and debate, and if his views are
incorrect, they will ultimately be shown to be incorrect, else we'd
better be prepared for an unpleasant future on Usenet.

