The specific case of topic restrictions was addressed in the recent
thread concerning a newspaper advertising section.  The relevant
court commentary stated that since the state agent had opened the
forum to the topic of X, it could not impose viewpoint restrictions
on advertisements under the topic of X.  I expect the trail articles
in that thread are probably still around, unless your server expires
articles at less than a week.

>    But my point was that even for topic limitations, where is it written
>    how the enforcement process works?  How am I ensured due process of
>    readers of a group think my posts are off topic?  Without such written
>    guidelines in place, I suspect (this is MHO) that the courts would site
