That is left to each site.  Usenet is international, and to have one process
for all sites would simply be foolish.  Obviously, state-owned sites would
need to observe certain guidelines that wouldn't be necessary at a private
site, but it is still their responsibility to address abuse in the manner
that they find best.  The only penalty from the rest of the net towards a
site that will not or can not keep from abusing the net is to have their
feed cut off.  This is almost always a good enough reason that even large
sites (such as aol.com) find ways to stop their users from abusing Usenet.
Note that PSI reacted quite strongly to reports that other admins were
starting to alias their site out from their feeds because they harbored
an active spammer.
