Subject: USENET is not a {limited} public forum
Date: 10 Jul 1994 00:26:01 -0400
Message-ID: <2vnt8p$ke7@panix3.panix.com>

The concept of {limited} public forum is a legal one.  In order for
something to be a {limited} public forum, it must have a legal
existence.  USENET has no legal existence; hence USENET is not a
{limited} public forum.

Each site (e.g. panix.com) might be considered to be a {limited}
public forum; however, that would have to be determined on a site-by-
site basis.  It's fairly clear to me that *.com would be a private
forum; *.gov likewise (at least, all the *.gov sites I know of are
limited to employees of a particular section of the government); and,
except for the freenets, *.edu is likewise not public.  And, of
course, all of the foreign domains don't have to care about whether or
not the US considers them public fora.

